{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghbsQSzSFR9ECwRamrYU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WHEsQJaC8hTU9rAuBXmqaK","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/vv/zyff93v5391cmw7j8mlcf1ym0000gn/T/wi-agent-ax5wxbuz/NOTES.md","content":"# Construction\n\n**Layer 1:** dr and dc are linear in the one-hot inputs. The weight is +col / -col on the goal / agent column (and the same with rows for dr). Four ReLU units compute p=relu(dc), q=relu(-dc), s=relu(dr) and t=relu(-dr). That gives |dc|=p+q and |dr|=s+t.\n\n**Layer 2:** identity pass-through of those 4 units. They are already ≥ 0, so the ReLU leaves them unchanged.\n\n**Output:** the logits are linear in p, q, s, t:\n- stay  = 1 - |dc| - |dr|\n- up    = -dr - |dc|\n- down  =  dr - |dc|\n- left  = -dc - |dr| + 0.5\n- right =  dc - |dr| + 0.5\n\nWhy this works (dr and dc are integers):\n- At the origin: stay = 1 > 0.5 = left/right > 0 = up/down.\n- Elsewhere: stay ≤ 0, while the correct move scores ≥ 0.5. For a horizontal move the score is |dc|-|dr|+0.5. For a vertical move with |dr|>|dc| it is |dr|-|dc| ≥ 1, while the horizontal moves score ≤ -0.5.\n- When |dc|=|dr|, the +0.5 makes horizontal win, which matches the expert's tie rule.\n- Each of the four direction logits is ≤ 0.5 whenever its direction is wrong.\n\nThe margin is at least 0.5 everywhere. The outputs are scaled ×10 for that, so the network should be 100% accurate.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3330,"cache_read_input_tokens":2254,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3330},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8640f512-2d03-4f60-a8a9-fbcc214246c7","uuid":"4a9f7b64-509e-4976-a673-97e3d3b4cfb1","timestamp":"2026-11-04T08:51:27.567Z","request_id":"req_011CghbsQ7exzyvvzM9BGM2v","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01WHEsQJaC8hTU9rAuBXmqaK":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/vv/zyff93v5391cmw7j8mlcf1ym0000gn/T/wi-agent-ax5wxbuz/NOTES.md","content":"# Construction\n\n**Layer 1:** dr and dc are linear in the one-hot inputs. The weight is +col / -col on the goal / agent column (and the same with rows for dr). Four ReLU units compute p=relu(dc), q=relu(-dc), s=relu(dr) and t=relu(-dr). That gives |dc|=p+q and |dr|=s+t.\n\n**Layer 2:** identity pass-through of those 4 units. They are already ≥ 0, so the ReLU leaves them unchanged.\n\n**Output:** the logits are linear in p, q, s, t:\n- stay  = 1 - |dc| - |dr|\n- up    = -dr - |dc|\n- down  =  dr - |dc|\n- left  = -dc - |dr| + 0.5\n- right =  dc - |dr| + 0.5\n\nWhy this works (dr and dc are integers):\n- At the origin: stay = 1 > 0.5 = left/right > 0 = up/down.\n- Elsewhere: stay ≤ 0, while the correct move scores ≥ 0.5. For a horizontal move the score is |dc|-|dr|+0.5. For a vertical move with |dr|>|dc| it is |dr|-|dc| ≥ 1, while the horizontal moves score ≤ -0.5.\n- When |dc|=|dr|, the +0.5 makes horizontal win, which matches the expert's tie rule.\n- Each of the four direction logits is ≤ 0.5 whenever its direction is wrong.\n\nThe margin is at least 0.5 everywhere. The outputs are scaled ×10 for that, so the network should be 100% accurate.\n"}}}
